        "## 20.6 Macro, micro, and weighted averaging\n",
        "\n",
        "For multiclass classification, we can compute precision, recall, and $F_1$ separately for each class.\n",
        "For class $c$, treat $c$ as positive and all other classes as negative.\n",
        "This gives $F_{1,c}$.\n",
        "\n",
        "Macro averaging gives equal weight to each class:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "F_{1,\\text{macro}} = \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{c=1}^K F_{1,c}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Weighted averaging weights each class by its support $n_c$:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "F_{1,\\text{weighted}} = \\sum_{c=1}^K \\frac{n_c}{n}F_{1,c}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Micro averaging pools all true positives, false positives, and false negatives across classes before computing the score.\n",
        "For single-label multiclass classification, micro $F_1$ equals accuracy.\n",
        "\n",
        "The choice matters.\n",
        "Macro $F_1$ emphasizes minority classes.\n",
        "Weighted $F_1$ is closer to the empirical class distribution.\n",
        "Micro metrics emphasize overall instance-level performance."
      ],
      "id": "45371563"
    },
