        "\n",
        "## 20.10 Overlap metrics for generated text\n",
        "\n",
        "Generated text is difficult to evaluate because there may be many correct answers.\n",
        "For example, two summaries can be semantically similar while sharing few exact words.\n",
        "Nevertheless, overlap metrics remain useful as quick baselines.\n",
        "\n",
        "Let $G$ be a generated sequence and $R$ be a reference sequence.\n",
        "For a token $n$-gram $g$, let $c_G(g)$ and $c_R(g)$ be its counts.\n",
        "A clipped precision score is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P_n = \\frac{\\sum_g \\min\\{c_G(g),c_R(g)\\}}{\\sum_g c_G(g)}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "BLEU-style evaluation combines clipped $n$-gram precisions with a brevity penalty.\n",
        "A simplified version is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{BLEU}_N = BP \\cdot \\exp\\left(\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{n=1}^N \\log P_n\\right),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "BP = \\begin{cases}\n",
        "1, & |G| > |R|,\\\\\n",
        "\\exp(1-|R|/|G|), & |G| \\le |R|.\n",
        "\\end{cases}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "ROUGE-style evaluation often emphasizes recall.\n",
        "For unigrams, a simple ROUGE-1 recall score is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{ROUGE\\text{-}1\\ recall} = \\frac{\\sum_g \\min\\{c_G(g),c_R(g)\\}}{\\sum_g c_R(g)}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The conceptual difference is important:\n",
        "\n",
        "- BLEU-style precision asks: how much of the generated text is supported by the reference?\n",
        "- ROUGE-style recall asks: how much of the reference was covered by the generated text?"
      ],
