        "## 20.11 Semantic evaluation and embedding similarity\n",
        "\n",
        "Exact token overlap fails when two answers are semantically similar but lexically different.\n",
        "A common alternative is to embed generated and reference text into vectors:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "z_G = f(G), \\qquad z_R = f(R),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "and score similarity by cosine similarity:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{sim}(G,R)=\\frac{z_G^T z_R}{\\|z_G\\|\\|z_R\\|}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This is mathematically clean but not automatically reliable.\n",
        "The embedding model itself has limitations.\n",
        "It may miss precise mathematical distinctions, factual errors, negations, or numerical mistakes.\n",
        "\n",
        "For example, the sentences\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "The null hypothesis is rejected.\n",
        "The null hypothesis is not rejected.\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "may be close in embedding space because most words are shared, but their statistical meanings are different.\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus semantic similarity is useful, but it should not replace task-specific correctness checks.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 20.12 Retrieval and RAG evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "For retrieval, the model returns an ordered list of documents\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "(d_1,d_2,\\ldots,d_k).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Let $R(q)$ be the set of relevant documents for query $q$.\n",
        "Precision@$k$ is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{Precision@}k = \\frac{|\\{d_1,\\ldots,d_k\\}\\cap R(q)|}{k}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Recall@$k$ is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{Recall@}k = \\frac{|\\{d_1,\\ldots,d_k\\}\\cap R(q)|}{|R(q)|}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The reciprocal rank is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "RR(q)=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{rank of first relevant document}}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The mean reciprocal rank is the average over queries:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{MRR}=\\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{j=1}^m RR(q_j).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "If relevance has graded scores, discounted cumulative gain is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{DCG@}k = \\sum_{i=1}^k \\frac{2^{rel_i}-1}{\\log_2(i+1)}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Normalized DCG divides by the ideal DCG:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{nDCG@}k = \\frac{\\operatorname{DCG@}k}{\\operatorname{IDCG@}k}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### RAG-specific decomposition\n",
        "\n",
        "A RAG system should be evaluated in at least three pieces:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{RAG quality} = \\text{retrieval quality} + \\text{grounding quality} + \\text{answer quality}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Retrieval quality asks whether useful evidence was retrieved.\n",
        "Grounding quality asks whether the answer is supported by the retrieved evidence.\n",
        "Answer quality asks whether the final response is correct, complete, and usable.\n",
        "\n",
        "A failure may occur at any stage:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. the retriever misses the relevant document;\n",
        "2. the retriever finds it but ranks it too low;\n",
        "3. the generator ignores the evidence;\n",
        "4. the generator cites evidence incorrectly;\n",
        "5. the answer is correct but incomplete;\n",
        "6. the answer is fluent but unsupported."
