        "\n",
        "If lower loss is better, then $d_i>0$ means B is better on item $i$.\n",
        "The mean difference is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\bar d = \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^n d_i.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "A paired comparison is usually better than comparing two independent averages because both models are evaluated on the same items.\n",
        "The paired standard error is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "SE(\\bar d)=\\frac{s_d}{\\sqrt n}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where $s_d$ is the sample standard deviation of the item-level differences."
