        "## 20.21 Common mistakes\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Reporting one number without uncertainty.** A score on a small test set may not be stable.\n",
        "2. **Comparing perplexity across different tokenizers.** Tokenization changes the unit of measurement.\n",
        "3. **Using accuracy on imbalanced data.** High accuracy may hide poor minority-class performance.\n",
        "4. **Treating overlap metrics as semantic correctness.** Word overlap does not guarantee meaning.\n",
        "5. **Ignoring retrieval in RAG evaluation.** A good answer may be impossible if retrieval failed.\n",
        "6. **Optimizing the test set.** Repeated test-set use biases reported performance.\n",
        "7. **Not examining errors.** Aggregate metrics rarely reveal all failure modes.\n",
        "8. **Using an AI judge without validation.** The evaluator must also be evaluated.\n",
